WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.377 --> 00:00:02.334
(laughing)

00:00:02.334 --> 00:00:04.638
- [Man] Liquid Ass is a stinky liquid

00:00:04.638 --> 00:00:09.556
that smells like butt crack
with hints of dead animal.

00:00:09.556 --> 00:00:11.264
- [Narrator] So, there are these guys.

00:00:11.264 --> 00:00:13.389
- Andrew Masters, I make Liquid Ass.

00:00:13.389 --> 00:00:16.807
- Allen Wittman, Liquid Ass
creator and head janitor.

00:00:16.807 --> 00:00:20.422
- We make the world's best stink product.

00:00:20.422 --> 00:00:21.874
- [Narrator] And they work here.

00:00:21.874 --> 00:00:24.352
- [Allen] This is what
we call the Ass Factory.

00:00:24.352 --> 00:00:26.024
- [Narrator] They hated their jobs,

00:00:26.024 --> 00:00:27.981
so they followed their dreams and started

00:00:27.981 --> 00:00:29.983
a successful prank product company,

00:00:29.983 --> 00:00:33.566
specializing in a really
rancid fart spray.

00:00:35.196 --> 00:00:37.214
But they needed a name.

00:00:37.214 --> 00:00:38.765
- I said, "So, what we gonna name it?"

00:00:38.765 --> 00:00:40.499
And he's getting ready
to sit down and he goes,

00:00:40.499 --> 00:00:41.510
"I don't know, Liquid Ass?"

00:00:41.510 --> 00:00:42.938
And I'm like, "That's it."

00:00:42.938 --> 00:00:45.438
(funny music)

00:00:47.216 --> 00:00:49.353
- [Narrator] Then
something curious happens.

00:00:49.353 --> 00:00:50.942
- [Allen] We're making
a product specifically

00:00:50.942 --> 00:00:53.832
for pranks at first, but
then we start getting calls

00:00:53.832 --> 00:00:56.195
from military people.

00:00:56.195 --> 00:00:58.276
- [Narrator] Enter Stu Segall, this guy.

00:00:58.276 --> 00:01:01.520
- Stu ordered from us,
and I'd never met Stu.

00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:02.356
It sounds like he's got a,

00:01:02.356 --> 00:01:04.117
you know, a pretty neat business.

00:01:04.117 --> 00:01:05.692
- [Narrator] He really does.

00:01:05.692 --> 00:01:09.086
- And he’d come up with the
idea to use it for a triage,

00:01:09.086 --> 00:01:11.456
but the fact is that it
goes from prank product

00:01:11.456 --> 00:01:14.300
to medical field is sort of a,

00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:15.550
sort of a jump.

00:01:17.587 --> 00:01:19.138
- [Narrator] Turns out
there's a secondary market

00:01:19.138 --> 00:01:21.606
for this stuff, training
some of the most elite

00:01:21.606 --> 00:01:24.297
armed forces to do their jobs.

00:01:24.297 --> 00:01:27.046
- We are a company that
replicates the environment

00:01:27.046 --> 00:01:29.782
of combat and right now we are in a set

00:01:29.782 --> 00:01:32.737
that we built for medical training.

00:01:32.737 --> 00:01:33.570
- Woah.

00:01:33.570 --> 00:01:34.403
- Oof.

00:01:35.411 --> 00:01:36.244
- Woah!

00:01:36.244 --> 00:01:38.779
- [Narrator] Basically,
before this prank fart spray,

00:01:38.779 --> 00:01:41.659
some of our best troops
and emergency medics

00:01:41.659 --> 00:01:44.008
were going into the field
completely unfamiliar

00:01:44.008 --> 00:01:46.552
with the overwhelmingly
horrid smells of death

00:01:46.552 --> 00:01:48.806
and disembowelment that they
would probably encounter

00:01:48.806 --> 00:01:50.840
as part of their jobs.

00:01:50.840 --> 00:01:52.559
- It's a very awful smell.

00:01:52.559 --> 00:01:54.710
It's something that
could actually gag a maggot

00:01:54.710 --> 00:01:56.316
as far as I'm concerned.

00:01:56.316 --> 00:01:58.810
It just smells like Liquid Ass.

00:01:58.810 --> 00:02:00.685
- [Narrator] Back to these two jokers.

00:02:00.685 --> 00:02:02.165
- [Allen] Now we have a product out there

00:02:02.165 --> 00:02:06.466
that's helping military
training, which is great.

00:02:06.466 --> 00:02:10.633
- [Narrator] You know,
not all heroes wear capes.

